Primary source: automateyournetwork/netclaw (Apache-2.0)
URL: https://github.com/automateyournetwork/netclaw

nmap-scanning is the authorised, defensive nmap ops skill, CONSOLIDATING three netclaw nmap MCP-tool skills
into one vault skill (SKILL + 3 references). Apache-2.0 primary (matching the netclaw source licence). It
produces the running-service + version data that nvd-cve looks up and vulnerability-management prioritises.
VulnMgmt + ASM family PR 3 of 4 (Apache open-source tools).

Files folded (3 netclaw skills -> 1 vault skill) -> reference mapping:
  netclaw workspace/skills/nmap-network-scan/SKILL.md (host discovery + port scanning: ping/ARP, SYN/TCP/
    UDP/top-ports, scope enforcement, audit logging)
  netclaw workspace/skills/nmap-service-detection/SKILL.md (service fingerprinting, OS detection, NSE
    scripts, vuln NSE category, full recon)
  netclaw workspace/skills/nmap-scan-management/SKILL.md (custom scans with injection/output-flag blocking,
    scan history, before/after comparison)
    -> SKILL.md (condensed core: authorised + scoped + logged; discover hosts before scanning ports; match
       the technique to the need; detection adds the why; persist and compare; classification; router;
       authorised-use boundary)
    -> references/host-and-port-scanning.md (ping + ARP host discovery, SYN/TCP/UDP/top-N port scanning,
       commands + flags + privileges, a typical subnet sweep, output)
    -> references/service-and-vuln-detection.md (service version detection -sV, OS fingerprinting -O, NSE
       scripts + common script names, the vuln NSE category, full recon sweep, handoff to nvd-cve)
    -> references/scope-and-management.md (CIDR-allowlist scope enforcement, audit logging, custom scans +
       injection/output-flag blocking, scan history, before/after change comparison)

Customisations: netclaw MCP-bound plumbing ($MCP_CALL / $NMAP_MCP_SCRIPT tool invocations, openclaw
metadata, user-invocable frontmatter) genericised to plain nmap commands/flags usable outside the netclaw
harness; the three upstream skills merged into one consolidated skill (network-scan + service-detection +
scan-management); DEFENSIVE / AUTHORISED-USE framing made prominent (scope enforcement + audit logging are
the core model, dual-use tool kept inside authorised/defensive context per the security policy); four-field
frontmatter (license Apache-2.0) + skill marker; references headerless (line 1 is # Title); em-dash /
en-dash purge (byte-scan == 0); British / Pacific English; ASCII -> arrows. Cross-refs nvd-cve +
vulnerability-management + attack-surface-management + network-detection-response (detection of scanning) +
acl-rule-analysis + the firewall-audit skills + secrets-hygiene.
